<<<
Womanly is used only to describe qualities peculiar to (a) good women as opposed to men (w. compassion, sympathy, intuition, &c.) or (b) developed women as opposed to girls (w. beauty, figure, experience).
===
*Womanly* is used only to describe qualities peculiar to (a) good women as opposed to men (*w. compassion, sympathy, intuition*, &c.) or (b) developed women as opposed to girls (*w. beauty, figure, experience*).
>>>

